The jungle was once ruled by a ferocious lion who daily devoured one animal from the kingdom. Everyone was scared of the lion and feared when their chance would come to go into the lion’s stomach. All the animals lived in constant terror until the clever little hare received the order to present himself in front of the lion. The clever hare devised a plant to save himself and other animals. The hare took very long to reach the lion and told him about another lion who sought kinghood. The lion growled with anger and  asked the hare to guide him to confront his opposing king. The hare brought him to a deep well after pointing out that his prey dwelled beneath them. The reflection in the well astounded the lion when he saw himself but his attempt at fighting his own image led to his demise in the water.
